{
  "abstract": "This is a Lean 4 formalization of Theorems 1.1 and 1.4 from the paper \"Diameter-free reverse inequalities and superorthogonality\" by A. Cushman, C. Demeter and S. Wu.\nTheorem 1.1 is a reverse square-function estimate in L^4 under a superorthogonality hypothesis that is weaker than the Type IV superorthogonality of Gressman-Pierce-Roos-Yung.\nTheorem 1.4 applies a similar estimate to the three-dimensional light cone, yielding a refinement of the reverse cone square-function estimate of Guth-Wang-Zhang.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Joris Roos"
    }
